  "solution": {
    "text": "For interference, by Young's double slits, the path difference is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext>xd</mtext><mtext>D</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>nλ</mi></math> for bright fringes and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext>xd</mtext><mtext>D</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> for dark fringes.<br /><br />The central fringes when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, coincide for all wavelengths.<br /><br />It is known that the third fringe of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>590</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>&nbsp;coincides with the fourth bright fringe of unknown wavelength&nbsp;<math><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></math>.<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>xd</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>D</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mo>×</mo> <mn>5</mn> <mn>9</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mtext>&nbsp;nm</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> <mo>×</mo> <mi>λ</mi> <mtext>&nbsp;nm</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mi>λ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mo>×</mo> <mn>5</mn> <mn>9</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> <mn>4</mn> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>5</mn> <mtext>&nbsp;nm</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
